## General Overview of the Project
To develop a comprehensive web application named 'VirtualBookPublishing' that allows users to publish virtual books, showcasing their content and author details, with no SQL database requirements, utilizing a local text document for data storage.

## Software Functional Requirements
1. Users shall be able to create a new book by entering a title, author, and content on the Create New Book Page.
2. Users shall be able to submit the book's information to be saved or cancel the creation and return to the Dashboard Page.
3. Users shall be able to view a list of their published books on the My Books Page.
4. Users shall be able to view the details of any book by clicking the View button next to each book in the list on the My Books Page.
5. Users shall be able to see the title, author, and content of a selected book on the Book Details Page.
6. Users shall be able to navigate back to the My Books Page from the Book Details Page.

## Data Storage
Data will be stored in local text files. Different types of data will be stored in separate `.txt` files. This structured data storage will facilitate easy data retrieval and management through simple file manipulations in Python, ensuring the application remains light and efficient without the need for a SQL database.

## Related Files
